The native cut is generic in H and accepts a shared reference to the SAME Verified. It selects sem.claims[point][lane], sem.extra[lane], sem.before_z1[lane], or field(y1,lane).c0 exactly as frozen verifier lines59-60. It selects g[lane] from the SAME borrowed fixed array. No compact expansion or semantic-finish surrogate is supplied.

Unlike NGU's fixed unread fixture fields, NGY quantifies roots, every challenge including zc, alpha, all three claims rows, extra, before_z1, state_before_z0, both circle points, transcript state, next_row and the concrete hash payload. All raw u32/u8/usize patterns here are Rust representation-valid. Arithmetic canonicality is deliberately not required to establish the native control/log identity; it is derived at child installation from the SAME root domain and invariant. Private Dot fields are constructed and projected only by cfg(kani) helpers in their declaring modules. All eight u64 sums and count vary independently, before and after, on both Result arms.

The source cut and hand reference never inspect H, transcript, roots, challenges, alpha, state_before_z0 or z. They have no mutable reference to any part of Verified, y1 or g. The only mutable borrows available to the safe local oracle are Dot and Log; its post assignment covers precisely Dot.c0.sums, Dot.c1.sums and Dot.count. Native proof_for_contract specifies modifies() on the wrapper's external inputs, which are shared. The actual Dot is wrapper-owned and its complete final state is returned and compared to f_ref. Rust borrowing/frame semantics and the existing std/allocator/ABI/compiler/P6 interpretation are retained trust; no address/byte-pointer equality is substituted for ownership.

H generality: the source and reference signatures quantify H:Digest32. The concrete harness uses Hash(u64), with arbitrary payload, to instantiate native execution. The generic source footprint does not call digest, clone H, move H, drop H, or access H. The extension to every caller's H therefore fixes no H value or observable field: the carrier is passed unchanged by shared reference, and all field projections have the same generic definitions. This is a source-parametric frame justification, recorded as part of reviewed transcription/P6, not a Kani quantification over Rust types.

